@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# A second worked example for the agent-provenance vocabulary
# (backlog/ontology/agentprov-vocabulary.ttl, issue #326), distilling the
# REAL reasoning from PR #328
# (https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/328), which closed issue
# #307 ("SHACL complex sh:path property paths"). Written for issue #334 (a
# sub-issue of the agent-provenance epic #306), per
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md's authoring convention --
# this is also the fixture that proves tests/provenance_queries.rs's
# glob-based loader picks up a NEW summary file automatically, with no test
# code change (see that guidelines doc's worked-example section).
#
# ghpull:328 is asserted as a bl:PullRequest/bl:WorkItem (reusing the
# backlog# vocabulary's own convention -- real GitHub URL as IRI) purely so
# agp:reasoningFor has a real bl:WorkItem to point at, per
# bl:RequiresWorkItemTypeShape and agentprov-shapes.ttl's sh:class
# bl:WorkItem check on agp:reasoningFor -- it is not a full backlog/
# snapshot entry. ghissues:307 (the issue this PR closed) is referenced
# only as an object (bl:closesIssue, prov:used), deliberately never typed
# bl:Issue -- typing it would subject it to
# bl:IssueIsEpicXorHasParentShape, which is out of scope for this
# grounding fixture (mirrors pr-300.ttl's identical choice for
# ghissues:264).
#
# session:pr328's startedAtTime/endedAtTime are real, taken from
# `gh pr view 328 --json commits,mergedAt`: startedAtTime is the final
# implementation commit's authoredDate (2026-07-31T21:39:51Z), endedAtTime
# is the PR's actual mergedAt (2026-07-31T22:01:33Z).

ghpull:328 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "shacl: complex sh:path property paths (inverse/sequence/alternative/quantified)" ;
    bl:number 328 ;
    bl:state bl:Closed ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:307 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr328 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:307 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-07-31T21:39:51Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-07-31T22:01:33Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr328Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "shacl/src/shapes.rs did not parse sh:inversePath, sequence paths, sh:alternativePath, or the quantified sh:zeroOrMorePath/sh:oneOrMorePath/sh:zeroOrOnePath forms at all -- ParsedPropShape::path was a plain IRI String. Added a new shacl/src/path.rs module with an ShPath AST parsed from sh:path's RDF object structure, plus path::pairs (shared subject/object extension computation mirroring sparql_parser's property-path reachability semantics), path::values_from (read-only per-focus-node evaluation for sh:not/sh:and/sh:or inner shapes), and path::resolve_one_path (materializes a compound path's extension as synthetic ground triples in translate.rs's Datalog working store, so existing rule-generation code needed no further changes). Two subtleties surfaced only once real fixtures were run: parse_path's cycle guard needed to be a DFS-stack (push/pop) rather than a permanent \"ever seen\" set, since a path can legitimately reuse one blank node in two positions; and an RDF-list reading of a sh:path node must take precedence over sh:inversePath/etc. when a node structurally satisfies both, per the suite's \"strange path\" fixtures. All 12 previously-skipped W3C core/path fixtures now pass." ;
    agp:abstractText "Added shacl/src/path.rs to parse and evaluate compound sh:path forms (inverse, sequence, alternative, quantified) -- 12 W3C fixtures now pass." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:328 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr328 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
